{"name":"Shady Lady","hex":"#9f9b9d","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shady","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Abounding in shades.","Causing shade."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shady"},{"term":"lady","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The mistress of a household.","A woman of breeding or higher class, a woman of authority."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To address as “lady”."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lady"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shady Lady (1945 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Shady Lady is a 1945 American romantic comedy film directed by George Waggner and starring Charles Coburn, Robert Paige, and Ginny Simms. Waggner originally offered Susanna Foster a starring role which she refused. Ginny Simms sings floor show songs \"Cuddle Up a Little Closer\", \"In Love With Love\" and \"Xango\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b7/Shady_Lady_%281945_film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shady_Lady_(1945_film)","wikidata":"Q17112973"},{"title":"Shady Lady (aircraft)","blocks":[{"text":"Shady Lady was a Consolidated B-24 Liberator aircraft that in August 1943 flew one of World War II's longest bombing missions, from Darwin in Australia to the oil refineries at Balikpapan in the East Kalimantan province on the island of Borneo, Indonesia."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shady_Lady_(aircraft)","wikidata":"Q7460938"},{"title":"Shady Lady (Ani Lorak song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Shady Lady\" is a song recorded by Ukrainian-born Russian singer Ani Lorak with music composed by Philipp Kirkorov and lyrics written by Karen Kavaleryan. It represented Ukraine in the Eurovision Song Contest 2008, held in Belgrade. She also released a Russian-language version of the song titled \"S neba v nebo\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/0b/Ani_LorakShadyLadycover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shady_Lady_(Ani_Lorak_song)","wikidata":"Q2597650"},{"title":"Lady","blocks":[{"text":"A lady is a woman who behaves in a polite way. Once used to describe only women of a high social class or status, the female counterpart of lord, now it may refer to any adult woman, as gentleman can be used for men."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lady","wikidata":"Q1378024"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/USAAF_Captain_Doug_Craig_1943.jpg/330px-USAAF_Captain_Doug_Craig_1943.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/USAAF_Captain_Doug_Craig_1943.jpg/330px-USAAF_Captain_Doug_Craig_1943.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"First Lieutenant Doug Craig","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUSAAF_Captain_Doug_Craig_1943.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Shady_Lady_14_August_1943.jpg/500px-Shady_Lady_14_August_1943.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Shady_Lady_14_August_1943.jpg/1280px-Shady_Lady_14_August_1943.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Shady_Lady_14_August_1943.jpg/500px-Shady_Lady_14_August_1943.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Shady Lady on the salt pan, August 1943","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AShady_Lady_14_August_1943.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Presidential_Citation_issued_for_the_Shady_Lady_crew_on_29_June_2011..jpg/500px-Presidential_Citation_issued_for_the_Shady_Lady_crew_on_29_June_2011..